+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Stock mutations currently do not reliably follow the ordered product, and stock is not restored when orders are canceled. This permits carts and orders that cannot be fulfilled and exposes products as purchasable after their stock reaches zero.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Make the product quantity shown by the v2 product API the authoritative stock for cart validation, checkout reservation, and cancellation restoration.
+- Validate every cart creation and quantity update atomically against current stock, returning HTTP 409 for an over-stock request while preserving the prior cart.
+- Validate and decrement each ordered product exactly once during both authenticated and anonymous checkout; reject the whole checkout with HTTP 409 when any line is short.
+- Restore each canceled order line to its product stock exactly once and reject transitions away from an already-canceled order with HTTP 409.
+- Derive API `available` and `canBePurchased` from positive stock plus the merchant availability flag.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `product-stock-lifecycle`: Consistent stock validation, reservation, restoration, and stock-derived purchase availability across the shopping lifecycle.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The cart facade and v1 cart/order APIs, order status handling, product read mapping, and product inventory persistence are affected. The change should preserve existing order and cart payloads while adding the specified 409 conflict behavior.
