+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Stock service and product read model
+
+- [x] 1.1 Trace the v2 product quantity mapping and implement a shared stock validation/mutation path keyed by product identity; verify unit tests prove decrement and restoration affect only the addressed product.
+- [x] 1.2 Make v2 `available` and `canBePurchased` depend on merchant availability and positive quantity; verify zero-stock, restock, and merchant-disabled product responses.
+
+## 2. Cart enforcement
+
+- [x] 2.1 Enforce stock limits when creating a cart or adding/merging a line, returning a mapped HTTP 409 and preserving the cart on failure; verify zero-stock and over-quantity requests.
+- [x] 2.2 Enforce stock limits for single and multi-line cart updates with validate-before-write atomicity while allowing lowering/removal; verify a mixed valid/invalid multi-update leaves every line unchanged.
+
+## 3. Checkout and order lifecycle
+
+- [x] 3.1 Validate all checkout lines before creating the order and decrement each matching product by its ordered quantity for both checkout endpoints; verify insufficient stock creates no order and success changes no unrelated product.
+- [x] 3.2 Restore stock on the first transition to CANCELED, make repeated cancellation idempotent, and reject transitions away from CANCELED with HTTP 409; verify all status paths and stock invariants.
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run the affected Maven module tests and a compile/package check for the complete multi-module build; verify the OpenSpec requirements and endpoint behavior are covered by passing tests.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the completed OpenSpec change after implementation and verification.
